cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or materials, please cite them as below."
title: "NAI (No-Ansatz Inference): experiments and reproduction materials"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Smirnov"
    given-names: "Mikhail"
    email: "lab@mindscan.org"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-30
abstract: >-
  Experiments with NAI, a symbolic-regression system that infers the functional
  form of a law from tabular data. Experiment 01: SLDBench, eight scaling-law
  discovery tasks (mean extrapolation R² 0.706 ± 0.026 over three replicates,
  without a language model). Experiment 02: a pre-registered test on open
  scaling-law data never seen by NAI, against the Chinchilla fit, a literature
  form and the PySR engine (mean R² 0.733 vs −0.412 for the PySR engine).
  Includes the NAI binary (public build), protocols, results and reproduction scripts.
keywords:
  - symbolic regression
  - scaling laws
  - extrapolation
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
license: CC-BY-4.0
